      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 2: Mean Comparisons (T-Tests & One-Way ANOVA)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921455883700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "*All Block 2 procedures (`One-Sample T-Test`, `Independent-Samples T-Test`, `Paired-Samples T-Test`, and `One-Way ANOVA`) support `Mt19937` Bootstrap resampling (`Percentile` & `BCa`, `Simple` & `Stratified`), verified in `bootstrap_golden_oracle::golden_oracle_independent_mean_diff` and `bootstrap_procedures_smoke.rs`.*"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455884500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 2.1. `ONE-SAMPLE T-TEST` (IBM Algorithms pp. 1061–1062)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_onesample.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_onesample.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `ttest_onesample::tests::test_golden_oracle_ttest_onesample_scipy`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  $$t = \\frac{\\bar{X} - \\text{TestValue}}{SE(\\bar{X})}, \\quad df = W - 1$$\n  $$p = I_{\\frac{df}{df + t^2}}\\left(\\frac{df}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}\\right)$$\n  $$\\text{CI} = (\\bar{X} - \\text{TestValue}) \\pm t_{1 - \\alpha/2, df} \\cdot SE(\\bar{X})$$\n  Student's $t$ critical quantiles $t_{crit}$ computed via Acklam's rational approximation refined by Newton-Raphson root finding.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455886000",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 2.2. `INDEPENDENT-SAMPLES T-TEST` (IBM Algorithms pp. 1058–1060)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_indep.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_indep.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `ttest_indep::tests::test_golden_oracle_against_scipy`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Levene's Test for Equality of Variances:** Canonical centering around group means:\n    $$Z_{kj} = |X_{kj} - \\bar{X}_k|, \\quad F = \\frac{MSB_Z}{MSW_Z}, \\quad df_1 = 1, \\; df_2 = n_1 + n_2 - 2$$\n  * **Equal Variances Assumed (Student's Pooled Variance):**\n    $$s_p^2 = \\frac{(n_1 - 1)s_1^2 + (n_2 - 1)s_2^2}{n_1 + n_2 - 2}, \\quad SE_{diff} = \\sqrt{s_p^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{n_1} + \\frac{1}{n_2}\\right)}, \\quad df = n_1 + n_2 - 2$$\n  * **Equal Variances Not Assumed (Welch's Separate Variance with Satterthwaite df):**\n    $$SE_{welch} = \\sqrt{\\frac{s_1^2}{n_1} + \\frac{s_2^2}{n_2}}, \\quad df = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{s_1^2}{n_1} + \\frac{s_2^2}{n_2}\\right)^2}{\\frac{(s_1^2/n_1)^2}{n_1 - 1} + \\frac{(s_2^2/n_2)^2}{n_2 - 1}}$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455887700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 2.3. `PAIRED-SAMPLES T-TEST` (IBM Algorithms pp. 1060–1061)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_paired.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/ttest_paired.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `ttest_paired::tests::test_paired_ttest_golden_oracle`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Pearson correlation with two-tailed significance $t_r = r \\sqrt{\\frac{n-2}{1-r^2}}$;\n  * Paired Differences $D_i = X_i - Y_i$:\n    $$t = \\frac{\\bar{D}}{SE(\\bar{D})}, \\quad df = n - 1, \\quad \\text{CI} = \\bar{D} \\pm t_{crit} \\cdot SE(\\bar{D})$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455889600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 2.4. `ONE-WAY ANOVA` (IBM Algorithms pp. 802–806)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/anova_oneway.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/anova_oneway.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** ANOVA integration suite\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Sums of squares:\n    $$BSS = \\sum_{l=1}^k n_l (\\bar{X}_l - \\bar{X})^2, \\quad WSS = \\sum_{l=1}^k \\sum_{j=1}^{n_l} (X_{lj} - \\bar{X}_l)^2, \\quad TSS = BSS + WSS$$\n  * Fisher's $F$-test: $F = \\frac{BSS / (k-1)}{WSS / (N-k)}$, with $p$-value derived from regularized incomplete beta;\n  * Multi-group Levene Test ($k$ groups) with $df_1 = k-1, \\; df_2 = N-k$.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455891500",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455892400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 3: Associations & Multivariates"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921455893100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 3.1. `CORRELATIONS` (IBM Algorithms pp. 193–194, 231, 752–753)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/correlations.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/correlations.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `correlations_tests::tests::test_spearman_and_kendall_oracle`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Pearson $r$:** $r = \\frac{\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})(y_i - \\bar{y})}{\\sqrt{\\sum(x_i - \\bar{x})^2 \\sum(y_i - \\bar{y})^2}}$ with significance $t = r \\sqrt{\\frac{n-2}{1-r^2}}, \\; df = n - 2$.\n  * **Spearman $\\rho$:** Pearson correlation over observation mid-ranks.\n  * **Kendall $\\tau_b$:** Rank correlation with complete tie handling (Kendall, 1955):\n    $$\\tau_b = \\frac{P - Q}{\\sqrt{(n_0 - T_X)(n_0 - T_Y)}}, \\quad n_0 = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}, \\quad T = \\sum \\frac{t_i(t_i-1)}{2}$$\n    Variance formulation incorporates all three tie correction components ($v_0, v_1, v_2$) with asymptotic two-tailed $Z = S / \\sqrt{Var(S)}$.\n  * **Bootstrap Resampling:** `Percentile` and `BCa` intervals for Pearson $r$, Spearman $\\rho$, and Kendall $\\tau_b$, verified in `bootstrap_golden_oracle::golden_oracle_pearson_correlation`.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455894600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 3.2. `REGRESSION LINEAR` (IBM Algorithms pp. 920–925)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/regression.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/regression.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `regression_tests::test_multiple_regression_golden_oracle`, `regression_tests::test_weighted_regression_golden_oracle`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Ordinary (OLS) and Weighted (WLS) Least Squares: Normal equations $(X^T W X) \\beta = X^T W Y$ solved via Gauss-Jordan matrix inversion with partial pivoting.\n  * Sum of squares partitioning: $SS_{Resid} = \\sum w_i (y_i - \\hat{y}_i)^2$, $SS_{Model} = SS_{Total} - SS_{Resid}$, $R^2 = 1 - \\frac{SS_{Resid}}{SS_{Total}}$.\n  * Adjusted $R^2$: $R^2_{adj} = 1 - (1 - R^2) \\frac{N - 1}{N - k}$.\n  * Model ANOVA $F$-test: $F = \\frac{MS_{Model}}{MS_{Resid}}, \\; df_1 = p, \\; df_2 = N - k$.\n  * Standardized Beta coefficients: $\\beta_j^* = b_j \\cdot \\frac{s_{X_j}}{s_Y}$.\n  * Multicollinearity diagnostics: Tolerance $Tol_j = 1 - R_j^2$ and Variance Inflation Factor $VIF_j = \\frac{1}{Tol_j}$.\n  * **Bootstrap Resampling:** Case and stratified resampling (`Percentile` & `BCa`) for unstandardized coefficients $B$, verified in `bootstrap_golden_oracle::golden_oracle_linear_regression_coefficients`.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455896400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 3.3. `FACTOR ANALYSIS / PCA` (IBM Algorithms pp. 428–442)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/factor.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/factor.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `factor_tests::test_factor_analysis_golden_oracle`, `factor_tests::test_jacobi_eigen_symmetric_known_matrix`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Correlation matrix decomposition via cyclic Jacobi rotations for exact eigenvalues $\\lambda_m$ and eigenvectors $V_m$.\n  * Component Loadings: $\\Lambda_{im} = \\sqrt{\\lambda_m} \\cdot V_{im}$, Communalities $h_i^2 = \\sum_{m=1}^M \\Lambda_{im}^2$.\n  * **Bartlett's Test of Sphericity:** $\\chi^2 = -\\left(N - 1 - \\frac{2p + 5}{6}\\right) \\ln |R|, \\quad df = \\frac{p(p-1)}{2}$.\n  * **Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin (KMO) Measure of Sampling Adequacy:**\n    $$KMO = \\frac{\\sum\\sum_{i \\ne j} r_{ij}^2}{\\sum\\sum_{i \\ne j} r_{ij}^2 + \\sum\\sum_{i \\ne j} a_{ij}^2}, \\quad a_{ij} = -\\frac{r^{ij}}{\\sqrt{r^{ii} r^{jj}}}$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455898200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 3.4. `RELIABILITY` (IBM Algorithms pp. 936–940)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/reliability.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/reliability.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `reliability_tests::test_reliability_golden_oracle_3_items`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Cronbach's Alpha (Cronbach, 1951):\n    $$\\alpha = \\frac{k}{k-1} \\left( 1 - \\frac{\\sum s_i^2}{s_{total}^2} \\right)$$\n  * Standardized Alpha based on average inter-item correlation $\\bar{r}$: $\\alpha_{std} = \\frac{k \\bar{r}}{1 + (k-1)\\bar{r}}$.\n  * Item-Deleted scale statistics:\n    $$s_{(i)}^2 = s_{total}^2 + s_i^2 - 2 Cov(X_i, X_{total}), \\quad \\alpha_{(i)} = \\frac{k-1}{k-2} \\left( 1 - \\frac{\\sum_{j \\ne i} s_j^2}{s_{(i)}^2} \\right)$$\n    $$r_{i(total-i)} = \\frac{Cov(X_i, X_{total}) - s_i^2}{\\sqrt{s_i^2 s_{(i)}^2}}$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455900100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455901100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 4: Nonparametric Tests"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921455901900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 4.1. `MANN-WHITNEY U TEST` (IBM Algorithms pp. 796–797)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_twosample.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_twosample.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `nonparam_twosample_tests::test_mann_whitney_oracle_no_ties`, `test_mann_whitney_oracle_with_ties`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Combined cases ranked with fractional mid-ranks for ties. Group rank sums $S_1, S_2$.\n  * Mann-Whitney $U$ statistics:\n    $$U_1 = S_1 - \\frac{n_1(n_1+1)}{2}, \\quad U_2 = S_2 - \\frac{n_2(n_2+1)}{2}, \\quad U = \\min(U_1, U_2)$$\n  * Wilcoxon $W$: rank sum for the group with smaller mean rank.\n  * Expected value and tie-corrected variance:\n    $$\\mu_U = \\frac{n_1 n_2}{2}, \\quad \\sigma_U^2 = \\frac{n_1 n_2}{12} \\left( (N + 1) - \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^m (t_i^3 - t_i)}{N(N - 1)} \\right)$$\n  * Asymptotic standard normal test: $Z = \\frac{U - \\mu_U}{\\sigma_U}$, two-tailed $p$-value $p = 2(1 - \\Phi(|Z|))$.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455903800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 4.2. `KRUSKAL-WALLIS ONE-WAY ANALYSIS OF VARIANCE` (IBM Algorithms pp. 800–801)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/kruskal_wallis.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/kruskal_wallis.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `kruskal_wallis_tests::test_kruskal_wallis_golden_oracle_distinct`, `test_kruskal_wallis_golden_oracle_ties`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Joint ranking of $N$ cases over $k$ groups with mid-ranks.\n  * Raw $H$ statistic:\n    $$H = \\frac{12}{N(N+1)} \\sum_{j=1}^k \\frac{R_j^2}{n_j} - 3(N+1)$$\n  * Tie correction factor and adjusted $H$:\n    $$H_{adj} = \\frac{H}{1 - \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^m (t_i^3 - t_i)}{N^3 - N}}$$\n  * Asymptotic significance: $\\chi^2$ survival function with $df = k - 1$.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455905800",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 4.3. `WILCOXON MATCHED-PAIRS SIGNED-RANK TEST` (IBM Algorithms p. 793)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_related.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_related.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `nonparam_related_tests::test_wilcoxon_signed_rank_oracle_with_ties`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Pairwise difference $D_i = Y_i - X_i$. Non-zero differences sorted by $|D_i|$ and ranked with mid-ranks.\n  * Positive sum $S_p = \\sum_{D_i > 0} R_i$, negative sum $S_n = \\sum_{D_i < 0} R_i$. Test statistic $W = \\min(S_p, S_n)$.\n  * Mean and tie-corrected variance:\n    $$\\mu_W = \\frac{n(n+1)}{4}, \\quad \\sigma_W^2 = \\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1) - 0.5 \\sum_{j=1}^l (t_j^3 - t_j)}{24}$$\n  * Continuity-corrected $Z$: $Z = \\frac{W - \\mu_W \\pm 0.5}{\\sigma_W}$, with asymptotic two-tailed $p$-value from standard normal.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455907700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 4.4. `SIGN TEST` (IBM Algorithms p. 792)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_related.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/nonparam_related.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `nonparam_related_tests::test_sign_test_oracle`, `test_sign_test_equal_halves`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Difference counts: positive $n_+$, negative $n_-$, total valid non-zero pairs $n = n_+ + n_-$, $k = \\min(n_+, n_-)$.\n  * Exact two-tailed binomial probability via regularized incomplete beta function:\n    $$p = 2 \\sum_{i=0}^k \\binom{n}{i} 0.5^n = 2 \\cdot I_{0.5}(n - k, k + 1)$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455909100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "---"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455910100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 5: Data Transformations and Imputations"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921455910700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 5.1. `RANK CASES` (IBM Algorithms pp. 904–906)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/rank_cases.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/rank_cases.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `rank_cases_tests::test_compute_ranks_no_ties`, `test_compute_ranks_with_ties`, `test_normal_scores`, `test_inv_normal_cdf_accuracy`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Ties methods: `MEAN` ($W_{i-1} + (w_i + 1)/2$), `LOW` ($W_{i-1} + 1$), `HIGH` ($W_i$), `SEQ` ($k+1$).\n  * Cumulative proportion estimators:\n    * **Blom (1958):** $F = \\frac{r - 3/8}{w + 1/4}$\n    * **Tukey (1962):** $F = \\frac{r - 1/3}{w + 1/3}$\n    * **Rankit:** $F = \\frac{r - 1/2}{w}$\n    * **Van der Waerden:** $F = \\frac{r}{w + 1}$\n  * **Normal Scores:** $Z = \\Phi^{-1}(F)$ computed using Peter J. Acklam's rational approximation ($\\le 1.15 \\times 10^{-9}$ error).\n  * Fractional ranks ($r / w$), Percent ($100 r / w$), and Ntiles ($\\lceil \\frac{r k}{w} \\rceil$).\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455912300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 5.2. `REPLACE MISSING VALUES` (IBM Algorithms pp. 66, 117, 143, 960)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/replace_missing.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/replace_missing.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `replace_missing::tests::test_linear_interpolation`, `test_linear_trend`, `test_mean_nearby_imputation`, `test_median_nearby_imputation`, `test_series_mean_imputation`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * **Linear Interpolation:** $y_i = y_0 + \\frac{i - i_0}{i_1 - i_0}(y_1 - y_0)$ between surrounding valid cases.\n  * **Series Mean:** $\\bar{y} = \\frac{1}{n_{valid}} \\sum y_i$.\n  * **Mean & Median of Nearby Points:** Symmetric span window $j \\in [\\max(0, i - span), \\min(n - 1, i + span)], j \\ne i$.\n  * **Linear Trend at Point:** Bivariate linear regression $y = a + b \\cdot t$ where $t$ is case sequence index.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455914100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 5.3. `OPTIMAL BINNING` (IBM Algorithms pp. 130, 816–826)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/optimal_binning.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/optimal_binning.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `optimal_binning::tests::test_perfect_two_class_split`, `test_null_handling`, `test_constant_feature`\n* **Mathematical Formula Verification:**\n  * Supervised discretization based on Fayyad & Irani (1993) Minimum Description Length Principle (MDLP) and Shannon entropy:\n    $$Ent(S) = - \\sum_{i=1}^k p_i \\log_2 p_i$$\n    $$Gain(S, T) = Ent(S) - \\frac{|S_1|}{|S|} Ent(S_1) - \\frac{|S_2|}{|S|} Ent(S_2)$$\n    $$MDLP \\; Stopping: Gain(S, T) > \\frac{\\log_2(N - 1)}{N} + \\frac{\\Delta(S, T)}{N}$$\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455915600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
