    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 9: Date & Time Wizard (`date_time.rs`)"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921455946900",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 9.1. Calendar Differences (`DATEDIFF`)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/date_time.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/date_time.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/date_time_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/date_time_cmd.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `date_time::tests::test_date_difference`, `tests::date_time_cmd_tests::test_date_time_cmd_diff`\n* **Mathematical & Calendar Invariants:**\n  * **Completed Units Truncation:** Canonical SPSS computes integer truncated intervals:\n    - **Years:** Completed calendar years between $(Y_1, M_1, D_1)$ and $(Y_2, M_2, D_2)$, adjusting downward if $(M_1, D_1) < (M_2, D_2)$ for $dt_1 > dt_2$.\n    - **Months:** $(Y_1 - Y_2) \\cdot 12 + (M_1 - M_2)$, with calendar day boundary compensation.\n    - **Weeks:** $\\lfloor \\frac{\\text{Days}(dt_1 - dt_2)}{7.0} \\rfloor$.\n    - **Days:** Calendar day difference $\\text{Date}(dt_1) - \\text{Date}(dt_2)$.\n    - **Hours, Minutes, Seconds:** Timestamp arithmetic. Note: `Seconds` returns exact epoch difference, while `Minutes` and `Hours` return continuous floating-point spans ($dt/60.0$, $dt/3600.0$) whereas SPSS syntax `DATEDIFF` defaults to integer truncated completed intervals.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Calendar & Algorithmic Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455948700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 9.2. Duration Increments & Date Arithmetic (`DATEADD`)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/date_time.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/date_time.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `date_time::tests::test_add_duration`\n* **Mathematical Invariants:**\n  * Calendar-aware addition (`checked_add_months`, leap-year February 29 handling, and end-of-month day clamping).\n  * Safely returns `SYSMIS` on arithmetic overflow or infinite/NaN interval amounts.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455950100",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 9.3. Component Extraction & Multi-Format Parsing (`XDATE.*`)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/date_time.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/date_time.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `date_time::tests::test_extract_parts`, `date_time::tests::test_parse_date_formats`\n* **Algorithmic Invariants:**\n  * **Extraction Targets:** Year, Month ($1..12$), Day ($1..31$), Hour ($0..23$), Minute ($0..59$), Second ($0..59$), DayOfWeek ($1..7$), Quarter ($1..4$).\n  * **SPSS Format Ingest:** Universal parser for ISO 8601 (`YYYY-MM-DD`, `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`), European (`DD.MM.YYYY`, `DD-MM-YYYY`), American (`MM/DD/YYYY`), and numeric epoch timestamps.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455951700",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
