    {
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Block 10: Recoding, Dummies & Value Counting"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_heading_1795702921455953400",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 10.1. Deterministic Recoding (`RECODE SAME / DIFFERENT`)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/recode.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/recode.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/recode_same_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/recode_same_cmd.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/recode_diff_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/recode_diff_cmd.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `recode::tests::test_exact_mapping`, `recode::tests::test_ranges_and_lowest_highest`, `recode::tests::test_missing_values_and_else`, `recode::tests::test_sps_formatting`, `tests::recode_cmd_tests::test_recode_same_and_undo`, `tests::recode_cmd_tests::test_recode_different_and_undo`\n* **Algorithmic Invariants:**\n  * **Ordered Evaluation:** Rules are checked strictly in order of declaration; the first matching rule dictates the resulting value.\n  * **Supported Match Clauses:** `Exact(v)`, `Range(low, high)` ($low \\le x \\le high$), `LOWEST THRU high`, `low THRU HIGHEST`, `SYSMIS`, `MISSING` (system or user missing), and `ELSE` (fallback).\n  * **Output Specifications:** `Value(v)`, `SYSMIS`, and `COPY` (preserve original value).\n  * **Full SPS Round-Trip:** `(1=10) (2 THRU 5=20) (LOWEST THRU 0=SYSMIS) (ELSE=COPY)`.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455955300",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 10.2. Automatic Recoding & Metadata Dictionary Synthesis (`AUTORECODE`)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/auto_recode.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/auto_recode.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/auto_recode_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/auto_recode_cmd.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `auto_recode::tests::test_auto_recode_numbers`, `auto_recode::tests::test_auto_recode_strings_lowest`, `auto_recode::tests::test_auto_recode_strings_highest`, `commands::auto_recode_cmd::tests::test_auto_recode_command_execution_and_undo`\n* **Algorithmic Invariants:**\n  * Maps distinct values into consecutive integers $\\{1, 2, \\dots, K\\}$.\n  * Directional sorting: `LowestValue` (ascending) or `HighestValue` (descending).\n  * Automatic `ValueLabels` dictionary synthesis: creates mappings $1 \\mapsto \\text{\"Category 1\"}$, $2 \\mapsto \\text{\"Category 2\"}$ preserving original category names in the dataset dictionary.\n  * System-missing and empty string values map safely to `SYSMIS` (null) without assignment.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455957200",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 10.3. Dummy Variable Generation (`CREATE DUMMIES`)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/dummies.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/dummies.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/dummy_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/dummy_cmd.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `dummies::tests::test_generate_dummies_numeric_all`, `dummies::tests::test_generate_dummies_omit_first`, `dummies::tests::test_generate_dummies_text`, `commands::dummy_cmd::tests::test_create_dummies_command_execute_and_undo`\n* **Mathematical Invariants:**\n  * **Indicator Function:** $D_{ik} = \\mathbb{I}(X_i = c_k) \\in \\{0.0, 1.0\\}$. Missing values assign $D_{ik} = \\text{SYSMIS}$.\n  * **Reference Category Omission:** Optional omission of reference baseline (`omit_first`) to eliminate multi-collinearity (the dummy variable trap) in linear regression.\n  * **Sanitized SPSS Identifiers:** Automatic alphanumeric name sanitization (e.g. `gender_1`, `gender_2`).\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
      "id": "blk_native_paragraph_1795702921455958600",
      "managed_by": "project_parser",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "#### 10.4. Value Occurrence Counting Across Variables (`COUNT VALUES`)\n* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/count_values.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/count_values.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/count_values_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/count_values_cmd.rs)\n* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `count_values::tests::test_compute_count_across_columns_basic`, `count_values::tests::test_compute_count_with_system_missing`, `count_values::tests::test_criterion_matches_range`, `commands::count_values_cmd::tests::test_count_values_execution_new_var_and_undo`\n* **Mathematical Invariants:**\n  * **Row-wise Aggregation:**\n    $$\\text{Count}_i = \\sum_{j=1}^M \\mathbb{I}(X_{ij} \\in \\mathcal{C})$$\n    where $\\mathcal{C}$ is a set of criteria containing exact numbers, exact strings, ranges $[low, high]$, `LOWEST THRU`, `THRU HIGHEST`, or `SYSMIS`.\n  * Fully vectorized evaluation across multiple columns; safely evaluates to integer count with 100% undo support in `CommandBus`.\n* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**"
      },
