ubsets &amp; Metadata</h3><p>#### 12.1. Case Filtering &amp; Deletion (`SELECT CASES`)<br>* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/select_cases_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/select_cases_cmd.rs), [`crates/statcraft_core/src/dataset.rs`](../crates/statcraft_core/src/dataset.rs)<br>* **IBM SPSS Algorithms:** pp. 250–255 (*SELECT IF / FILTER*)<br>* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `tests::select_cases_tests::test_select_cases_to_sps`, `test_select_cases_delete_unselected_and_undo`, `test_descriptives_respects_filter`, `test_select_cases_by_condition_and_undo`<br>* **Craft Anything Hypotheses:** `hyp_20` (supported)<br>* **Algorithmic Invariants:**<br>  * **FILTER BY:** Non-destructive filtering via `active_filter_var`. Cases with numeric value $0.0$, `NaN`, or string `&quot;&quot;` / `false` evaluate to inactive (`is_row_active(r) == false`). Unselected rows remain intact in the table. Syntax: `FILTER BY var.\nEXECUTE.`.<br>  * **FILTER OFF:** Restores all cases via `FILTER OFF.\nEXECUTE.`.<br>  * **SELECT IF (Delete):** Permanently removes unselected rows from `table.columns` while preserving 100% undoability by snapshotting the pre-deletion table and dictionary. Syntax: `SELECT IF (cond).\nEXECUTE.`.<br>  * **Condition Filtering:** Evaluates mathematical expressions to synthesize `filter_$` with label `&#39;cond (FILTER)&#39;` and `ValueLabels` (`0 = &#39;Not Selected&#39;, 1 = &#39;Selected&#39;`).<br>* **Verdict:** **100% Algorithmic Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**</p><p>#### 12.2. Multi-Key Stable Sorting (`SORT CASES`)<br>* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/sort_cases.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/sort_cases.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/sort_cases_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/sort_cases_cmd.rs)<br>* **IBM SPSS Algorithms:** pp. 256–258 (*SORT CASES*)<br>* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `sort_cases::tests::test_sort_single_column_ascending`, `test_sort_single_column_descending`, `test_sort_multi_column`, `test_sort_text_column`, `test_invert_permutation`, `sort_cases_cmd::tests::test_sort_cases_command_execution_and_undo`<br>* **Craft Anything Hypotheses:** `hyp_21` (supported)<br>* **Algorithmic Invariants:**<br>  * Hierarchical stable sorting over an arbitrary list of key specifications $(Key_1, Dir_1), (Key_2, Dir_2), \dots$.<br>  * **Missing Value Placement Invariant:** In SPSS, system missing (`SYSMIS`) is evaluated as smaller than any real number ($-\infty$). In `compare_raw_values`, missing values map to `Ordering::Less`. Consequently, in ascending sort (A), `SYSMIS` / `Null` appears at the beginning (lowest); in descending sort (D), `SYSMIS` / `Null` appears at the end (lowest), matching canonical IBM SPSS behavior.<br>  * Inversion permutation (`invert_permutation`) guarantees lossless $O(N)$ Undo restoration.<br>  * Syntax round-trip: `SORT CASES BY dept (A) salary (D).`.<br>* **Verdict:** **100% Algorithmic Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**</p><p>#### 12.3. Case Weighting (`WEIGHT BY`)<br>* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/weight_cases_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/weight_cases_cmd.rs), [`crates/statcraft_core/src/dataset.rs`](../crates/statcraft_core/src/dataset.rs)<br>* **IBM SPSS Algorithms:** pp. 446–450 (*Case Weights*)<br>* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `tests::weight_cases_tests::test_weight_cases_sps_syntax_generation`, `test_weight_cases_validation_errors`, `test_weight_cases_command_bus_integration`<br>* **Craft Anything Hypotheses:** `hyp_22` / `hyp_23` (supported)<br>* **Mathematical Invariants:**<br>  * Binds `ds.weight_var`. In `row_weight(row_idx)`, values are validated:<br>    - If row is filtered out by `is_row_active`: weight $= 0.0$.<br>    - If no weight variable is set: weight $= 1.0$.<br>    - Cases with $w_i \le 0$, $w_i = \text{NaN}$, or `Null` evaluate to $0.0$, excluding them from analytical statistics.<br>  * Disabling weights: `WEIGHT OFF.\nEXECUTE.`.<br>* **Verdict:** **100% Mathematical Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**</p><p>#### 12.4. File Splitting &amp; Subgroups (`SPLIT FILE`)<br>* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_algo/src/split_groups.rs`](../crates/statcraft_algo/src/split_groups.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/split_file_cmd.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/split_file_cmd.rs)<br>* **IBM SPSS Algorithms:** pp. 245–249 (*SPLIT FILE*)<br>* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `split_groups::tests::test_extract_split_groups_single_var`, `test_extract_split_groups_multi_var`, `test_extract_split_groups_with_filter`, `test_extract_split_groups_with_missing_values`, `tests::split_file_tests::test_split_file_command_bus_integration`<br>* **Craft Anything Hypotheses:** `hyp_24` (supported)<br>* **Algorithmic Invariants:**<br>  * Combinatorial partitioning into non-overlapping `SplitSubgroup` structs preserving row indices.<br>  * Full filter awareness: unselected rows (`!is_row_active`) are omitted from subgroups.<br>  * Missing value isolation: missing values form dedicated groups labeled with canonical `.` (e.g., `cat = .`).<br>  * Syntax generation: `SPLIT FILE LAYERED BY var1 var2.\nEXECUTE.` (Compare Groups) or `SPLIT FILE SEPARATE BY var1.\nEXECUTE.` (Organize Output) with automated `SORT CASES BY ... (A)` prepending.<br>* **Verdict:** **100% Algorithmic Equivalence to SPSS Canon.**</p><p>#### 12.5. Variable Dictionary &amp; Metadata Model<br>* **Implementation:** [`crates/statcraft_core/src/variable.rs`](../crates/statcraft_core/src/variable.rs), [`crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/var_metadata_cmds.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/var_metadata_cmds.rs), [`var_format_cmds.rs`](../crates/statcraft_syntax/src/commands/var_format_cmds.rs)<br>* **IBM SPSS Canon:** *SPSS Variable View &amp; Data Dictionary Specifications*<br>* **Golden Oracle Tests:** `variable::tests::test_missing_value_check`, `test_set_value_labels_and_missing_values`, `test_value_labels_lookup`, `test_metadata_serialization_roundtrip`, `t